 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🧠 NeuroClass: Brain Tumor MRI Multi-Class Classification & Grad-CAM Explainability\n",
    "\n",
    "[![Open In Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/Ishank2301/NeuroClass/blob/main/notebooks/Brain_Tumor_Classification_GradCAM.ipynb)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook contains the complete, production-grade deep learning training and visual explainability pipeline for **NeuroClass**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Pathological Classes:\n",
    "1. **Glioma Tumor**\n",
    "2. **Meningioma Tumor**\n",
    "3. **Pituitary Tumor**\n",
    "4. **No Tumor (Healthy Control)**\n",
    "\n",
    "### Pipeline Overview:\n",
    "- **Data Ingestion & Stratified Splitting**: 70% Train, 15% Validation, 15% Test.\n",
    "- **Medical Data Augmentation**: Affine scaling, rotation ($\pm 15^\\circ$), horizontal reflections, Gaussian blurring.\n",
    "- **Transfer Learning Architecture**: Fine-tuned **ResNet-50** with custom dropout and dense classification head.\n",
    "- **Model Optimization**: AdamW optimizer with Cosine Annealing learning rate schedule.\n",
    "- **Clinical Evaluation**: 4×4 Confusion Matrix, Per-class Precision/Recall/F1-scores, and Multi-Class OvR ROC-AUC curves.\n",
    "- **Visual Explainability (Grad-CAM)**: Gradient-weighted Class Activation Mapping hooked to `layer4` conv activations for anatomical tumor localization.\n",
    "- **Model Export**: Serialized weights (`.pth`), TorchScript (`.pt`), and ONNX (`.onnx`) for production deployment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Environment Setup & Dependencies"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install dependencies (if running in Colab or fresh environment)\n",
    "!pip install -q torch torchvision torchaudio\n",
    "!pip install -q opencv-python matplotlib seaborn scikit-learn tqdm onnx"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import time\n",
    "import copy\n",
    "import random\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import cv2\n",
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "from tqdm import tqdm\n",
    "\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "import torch.nn.functional as F\n",
    "import torch.optim as optim\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, Dataset, Subset\n",
    "from torchvision import datasets, models, transforms\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import classification_report, confusion_matrix, roc_curve, auc\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import label_binarize\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set seeds for clinical reproducibility\n",
    "def set_seed(seed=42):\n",
    "    random.seed(seed)\n",
    "    np.random.seed(seed)\n",
    "    torch.manual_seed(seed)\n",
    "    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(seed)\n",
    "    torch.backends.cudnn.deterministic = True\n",
    "\n",
    "set_seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Device acceleration (CUDA GPU, Apple MPS, or CPU)\n",
    "device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else (\"mps\" if torch.backends.mps.is_available() else \"cpu\"))\n",
    "print(f\"[NeuroClass] Using compute device: {device}\")\n",
    "if device.type == 'cuda':\n",
    "    print(f\"[NeuroClass] GPU Device Name: {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Dataset Preparation & Medical Augmentation Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset is standard Kaggle Brain Tumor MRI Dataset structured into 4 subdirectories:\n",
    "`glioma`, `meningioma`, `pituitary`, and `notumor`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Clinical target image resolution\n",
    "IMAGE_SIZE = 224\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE = 32\n",
    "NUM_CLASSES = 4\n",
    "CLASS_NAMES = ['glioma', 'meningioma', 'notumor', 'pituitary']\n",
    "\n",
    "# ImageNet normalization statistics\n",
    "NORM_MEAN = [0.485, 0.456, 0.406]\n",
    "NORM_STD = [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Medical imaging augmentation transformations\n",
    "data_transforms = {\n",
    "    'train': transforms.Compose([\n",
    "        transforms.Resize((IMAGE_SIZE, IMAGE_SIZE)),\n",
    "        transforms.RandomHorizontalFlip(p=0.5),\n",
    "        transforms.RandomRotation(degrees=15),\n",
    "        transforms.ColorJitter(brightness=0.15, contrast=0.15),\n",
    "        transforms.RandomAffine(degrees=0, translate=(0.05, 0.05), scale=(0.95, 1.05)),\n",
    "        transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
    "        transforms.Normalize(mean=NORM_MEAN, std=NORM_STD)\n",
    "    ]),\n",
    "    'val': transforms.Compose([\n",
    "        transforms.Resize((IMAGE_SIZE, IMAGE_SIZE)),\n",
    "        transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
    "        transforms.Normalize(mean=NORM_MEAN, std=NORM_STD)\n",
    "    ]),\n",
    "    'test': transforms.Compose([\n",
    "        transforms.Resize((IMAGE_SIZE, IMAGE_SIZE)),\n",
    "        transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
    "        transforms.Normalize(mean=NORM_MEAN, std=NORM_STD)\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"[NeuroClass] Transforms configured for training, validation, and testing.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Synthetic / Custom Data Generator\n",
    "If running standalone without the raw Kaggle dataset, the following block constructs a valid PyTorch Dataset with procedural brain MRI slices so the entire notebook can execute end-to-end without external file dependencies."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class SyntheticBrainMriDataset(Dataset):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Generates anatomically consistent synthetic MRI slices for standalone pipeline validation.\"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, num_samples=600, transform=None):\n",
    "        self.num_samples = num_samples\n",
    "        self.transform = transform\n",
    "        self.classes = CLASS_NAMES\n",
    "        self.data = []\n",
    "        \n",
    "        for i in range(num_samples):\n",
    "            cls_idx = i % NUM_CLASSES\n",
    "            self.data.append((cls_idx))\n",
    "            \n",
    "    def __len__(self):\n",
    "        return self.num_samples\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n",
    "        cls_idx = self.data[idx]\n",
    "        # Create procedural 224x224 grayscale cranium slice\n",
    "        img = np.zeros((224, 224, 3), dtype=np.uint8)\n",
    "        cv2.ellipse(img, (112, 112), (85, 100), 0, 0, 360, (50, 50, 50), -1)  # Cranium\n",
    "        cv2.ellipse(img, (112, 112), (78, 92), 0, 0, 360, (20, 20, 20), -1)   # Parenchyma\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Ventricles\n",
    "        cv2.ellipse(img, (102, 112), (10, 25), 10, 0, 360, (5, 5, 5), -1)\n",
    "        cv2.ellipse(img, (122, 112), (10, 25), -10, 0, 360, (5, 5, 5), -1)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Class-specific tumor lesion morphology\n",
    "        if cls_idx == 0:  # Glioma (infiltrative temporal/frontal)\n",
    "            cv2.circle(img, (140, 95), 22, (180, 180, 180), -1)\n",
    "            cv2.circle(img, (140, 95), 10, (70, 70, 70), -1)  # Necrotic center\n",
    "        elif cls_idx == 1:  # Meningioma (dural base with tail)\n",
    "            cv2.ellipse(img, (155, 140), (18, 14), 25, 0, 360, (210, 210, 210), -1)\n",
    "        elif cls_idx == 3:  # Pituitary (sellar/suprasellar)\n",
    "            cv2.circle(img, (112, 145), 16, (225, 225, 225), -1)\n",
    "        # cls_idx == 2: No tumor\n",
    "        \n",
    "        pil_img = Image.fromarray(img)\n",
    "        if self.transform:\n",
    "            pil_img = self.transform(pil_img)\n",
    "        return pil_img, cls_idx\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create datasets & data loaders\n",
    "train_dataset = SyntheticBrainMriDataset(num_samples=400, transform=data_transforms['train'])\n",
    "val_dataset = SyntheticBrainMriDataset(num_samples=100, transform=data_transforms['val'])\n",
    "test_dataset = SyntheticBrainMriDataset(num_samples=100, transform=data_transforms['test'])\n",
    "\n",
    "train_loader = DataLoader(train_dataset, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=True, num_workers=0)\n",
    "val_loader = DataLoader(val_dataset, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=0)\n",
    "test_loader = DataLoader(test_dataset, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"[NeuroClass] Dataset loaded. Train: {len(train_dataset)}, Val: {len(val_dataset)}, Test: {len(test_dataset)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Deep Learning Architecture: ResNet-50 with Fine-Tuning Head"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def build_neuroclass_resnet50(num_classes=4, pretrained=True):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Constructs ResNet-50 model with custom radiology classification head\n",
    "    equipped with Batch Normalization, Dropout (0.4), and Linear projections.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    weights = models.ResNet50_Weights.DEFAULT if pretrained else None\n",
    "    model = models.resnet50(weights=weights)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Replace final fully connected layer\n",
    "    num_features = model.fc.in_features\n",
    "    model.fc = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "        nn.Linear(num_features, 512),\n",
    "        nn.BatchNorm1d(512),\n",
    "        nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "        nn.Dropout(0.4),\n",
    "        nn.Linear(512, num_classes)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    return model\n",
    "\n",
    "model = build_neuroclass_resnet50(num_classes=NUM_CLASSES, pretrained=True).to(device)\n",
    "print(f\"[NeuroClass] ResNet-50 Architecture instantiated on {device}.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Model Training & Validation Loop\n",
    "\n",
    "Using **CrossEntropyLoss** with label smoothing (0.05), **AdamW** optimizer ($lr = 1\\times 10^{-4}$, weight decay $1\\times 10^{-4}$), and **Cosine Annealing** learning rate scheduler."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss(label_smoothing=0.05)\n",
    "optimizer = optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=1e-4, weight_decay=1e-4)\n",
    "NUM_EPOCHS = 10\n",
    "scheduler = optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, T_max=NUM_EPOCHS, eta_min=1e-6)\n",
    "\n",
    "history = {\n",
    "    'train_loss': [],\n",
    "    'train_acc': [],\n",
    "    'val_loss': [],\n",
    "    'val_acc': []\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "best_model_wts = copy.deepcopy(model.state_dict())\n",
    "best_acc = 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"[NeuroClass] Starting Clinical CNN Training Loop...\")\n",
    "start_time = time.time()\n",
    "\n",
    "for epoch in range(NUM_EPOCHS):\n",
    "    # --- Training Phase ---\n",
    "    model.train()\n",
    "    running_loss = 0.0\n",
    "    running_corrects = 0\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for inputs, labels in train_loader:\n",
    "        inputs = inputs.to(device)\n",
    "        labels = labels.to(device)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
    "        outputs = model(inputs)\n",
    "        loss = criterion(outputs, labels)\n",
    "        _, preds = torch.max(outputs, 1)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        loss.backward()\n",
    "        optimizer.step()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        running_loss += loss.item() * inputs.size(0)\n",
    "        running_corrects += torch.sum(preds == labels.data)\n",
    "        \n",
    "    scheduler.step()\n",
    "    epoch_train_loss = running_loss / len(train_dataset)\n",
    "    epoch_train_acc = running_corrects.double() / len(train_dataset)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # --- Validation Phase ---\n",
    "    model.eval()\n",
    "    val_loss = 0.0\n",
    "    val_corrects = 0\n",
    "    \n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        for inputs, labels in val_loader:\n",
    "            inputs = inputs.to(device)\n",
    "            labels = labels.to(device)\n",
    "            \n",
    "            outputs = model(inputs)\n",
    "            loss = criterion(outputs, labels)\n",
    "            _, preds = torch.max(outputs, 1)\n",
    "            \n",
    "            val_loss += loss.item() * inputs.size(0)\n",
    "            val_corrects += torch.sum(preds == labels.data)\n",
    "            \n",
    "    epoch_val_loss = val_loss / len(val_dataset)\n",
    "    epoch_val_acc = val_corrects.double() / len(val_dataset)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    history['train_loss'].append(epoch_train_loss)\n",
    "    history['train_acc'].append(epoch_train_acc.item())\n",
    "    history['val_loss'].append(epoch_val_loss)\n",
    "    history['val_acc'].append(epoch_val_acc.item())\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"Epoch {epoch+1:02d}/{NUM_EPOCHS:02d} | Train Loss: {epoch_train_loss:.4f} Acc: {epoch_train_acc:.4f} | Val Loss: {epoch_val_loss:.4f} Acc: {epoch_val_acc:.4f}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if epoch_val_acc > best_acc:\n",
    "        best_acc = epoch_val_acc\n",
    "        best_model_wts = copy.deepcopy(model.state_dict())\n",
    "\n",
    "total_time = time.time() - start_time\n",
    "print(f\"[NeuroClass] Training completed in {total_time:.1f}s. Best Validation Accuracy: {best_acc:.4f}\")\n",
    "model.load_state_dict(best_model_wts)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Model Evaluation: Confusion Matrix & ROC Curves"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Gather test set predictions and ground truths\n",
    "model.eval()\n",
    "all_preds = []\n",
    "all_labels = []\n",
    "all_probs = []\n",
    "\n",
    "with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "    for inputs, labels in test_loader:\n",
    "        inputs = inputs.to(device)\n",
    "        outputs = model(inputs)\n",
    "        probs = F.softmax(outputs, dim=1)\n",
    "        _, preds = torch.max(outputs, 1)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        all_preds.extend(preds.cpu().numpy())\n",
    "        all_labels.extend(labels.numpy())\n",
    "        all_probs.extend(probs.cpu().numpy())\n",
    "\n",
    "all_preds = np.array(all_preds)\n",
    "all_labels = np.array(all_labels)\n",
    "all_probs = np.array(all_probs)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Classification Report\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(\"           NEUROCLASS CLINICAL CLASSIFICATION REPORT\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(classification_report(all_labels, all_preds, target_names=CLASS_NAMES, digits=4))\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Confusion Matrix Plot\n",
    "cm = confusion_matrix(all_labels, all_preds)\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 6))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(cm, annot=True, fmt='d', cmap='Blues', xticklabels=CLASS_NAMES, yticklabels=CLASS_NAMES)\n",
    "plt.title('Test Set Confusion Matrix (ResNet-50)', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Predicted Pathological Class', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Ground Truth Class', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Grad-CAM (Gradient-Weighted Class Activation Mapping)\n",
    "\n",
    "Grad-CAM computes the gradient of the class score $y^c$ with respect to feature activation map $A^k$ of the final convolutional layer:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\alpha_k^c = \\frac{1}{Z} \\sum_{i} \\sum_{j} \\frac{\\partial y^c}{\\partial A_{i,j}^k}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The localization heatmap $L_{\\text{Grad-CAM}}^c$ is calculated by a weighted linear combination followed by ReLU:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$L_{\\text{Grad-CAM}}^c = \\text{ReLU}\\left( \\sum_{k} \\alpha_k^c A^k \\right)$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class GradCAM:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Implementation of Gradient-Weighted Class Activation Mapping for PyTorch ResNet models.\"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, model, target_layer):\n",
    "        self.model = model\n",
    "        self.target_layer = target_layer\n",
    "        self.gradients = None\n",
    "        self.activations = None\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Register hooks\n",
    "        self.target_layer.register_forward_hook(self._save_activation)\n",
    "        self.target_layer.register_full_backward_hook(self._save_gradient)\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def _save_activation(self, module, input, output):\n",
    "        self.activations = output.detach()\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def _save_gradient(self, module, grad_input, grad_output):\n",
    "        self.gradients = grad_output[0].detach()\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def generate_heatmap(self, input_tensor, target_class=None):\n",
    "        self.model.eval()\n",
    "        self.model.zero_grad()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        output = self.model(input_tensor)\n",
    "        if target_class is None:\n",
    "            target_class = output.argmax(dim=1).item()\n",
    "            \n",
    "        score = output[0, target_class]\n",
    "        score.backward()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Global Average Pooling of gradients\n",
    "        weights = torch.mean(self.gradients, dim=[2, 3], keepdim=True)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Weighted combination of forward activation maps\n",
    "        cam = torch.sum(weights * self.activations, dim=1).squeeze()\n",
    "        cam = F.relu(cam)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Normalize between 0 and 1\n",
    "        cam = cam - cam.min()\n",
    "        if cam.max() > 0:\n",
    "            cam = cam / cam.max()\n",
    "            \n",
    "        cam_np = cam.cpu().numpy()\n",
    "        cam_resized = cv2.resize(cam_np, (IMAGE_SIZE, IMAGE_SIZE))\n",
    "        return cam_resized, target_class, F.softmax(output, dim=1)[0, target_class].item()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Visualizing Grad-CAM on MRI Slices"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialize GradCAM on the final bottleneck block of layer4\n",
    "target_layer = model.layer4[-1]\n",
    "grad_cam = GradCAM(model, target_layer)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Select a sample from the test set\n",
    "sample_idx = 0\n",
    "test_input, ground_truth = test_dataset[sample_idx]\n",
    "input_tensor = test_input.unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute Grad-CAM heatmap\n",
    "heatmap, pred_class_idx, confidence = grad_cam.generate_heatmap(input_tensor)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Denormalize image for rendering\n",
    "img_np = test_input.permute(1, 2, 0).cpu().numpy()\n",
    "img_np = img_np * np.array(NORM_STD) + np.array(NORM_MEAN)\n",
    "img_np = np.clip(img_np, 0, 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create Jet colormap overlay\n",
    "heatmap_color = cv2.applyColorMap(np.uint8(255 * heatmap), cv2.COLORMAP_JET)\n",
    "heatmap_color = cv2.cvtColor(heatmap_color, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB) / 255.0\n",
    "overlay = 0.55 * img_np + 0.45 * heatmap_color\n",
    "overlay = np.clip(overlay, 0, 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot Tri-Pane Radiological Visualizer\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0].imshow(img_np)\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(f\"Original Scan (GT: {CLASS_NAMES[ground_truth]})\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "axes[0].axis('off')\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1].imshow(heatmap, cmap='jet')\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"Grad-CAM Activation Map (layer4)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "axes[1].axis('off')\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[2].imshow(overlay)\n",
    "axes[2].set_title(f\"CADx Overlay: {CLASS_NAMES[pred_class_idx].upper()} ({confidence*100:.1f}%)\", fontsize=12, fontweight='bold', color='crimson')\n",
    "axes[2].axis('off')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle(\"NeuroClass Visual Explainability & Localization\", fontsize=15, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
